Record scope: documentation reconciliation against source
`7f88f3fe1ab8ee6c7279fa8b64dce7de5afac453`, using existing local records only.
This document assigns no new overall score. Current full compatibility
acceptance remains open under [decision 0013](../decisions/0013-complete-parity-acceptance.md)
and the [architecture contract](architecture.md).

## How to read the evidence

- **Historical assessment:** a retained row label, result or closure statement
  from its cited source/configuration. Its original data and citations remain.
- **Verified in this reconciliation:** document identities, literal statement
  inventory and saved artifact consistency checked against the named source.
  Executed results keep their own recorded revision, instrument and scope.
- **Current acceptance unverified:** the records examined here do not establish
  the corresponding current candidate/runtime/reference/backend conclusion.
  This describes evidence scope, not absence of implementation.

The contract's behavior and proof requirements remain controlling. Its older
implementation annotations and the ledger's later row assessments disagree
in places, including P1.4.a/P1.5.a and E4.1.a/E4.2.a/E4.3.a/E4.4.a. These
annotations need their cited evidence interpreted per row; neither an old
"unported" annotation nor an unavailable source/capture establishes that the
current mechanism is missing.

