## Disposition of the old rollup

The ledger's former "67 proven / 0 unported" and "pass 67 / fail 0" count
primary labels over catalogued statement IDs. It collapses branches and
carries divergences as notes on primary proven rows. Its own P1.6.a,
R3.4.d and R3.6.a annotations retain unmeasured, unported-at-recording or
sampled-only branches. The aggregate therefore cannot certify every branch,
the complete architecture scope, current CI, or all supported profiles.
The original rollup is retained as a quoted historical assessment.

Future acceptance updates should attach the exact candidate/checker/reference,
data/profile/backend, raw outcomes and independent review for the stated
scope. Historical rows are promoted only to the extent those receipts support;
unavailable evidence remains unverified rather than being relabelled missing
implementation. This applies the existing governance and adds no new product
implementation requirement.
